 "waiver_targets": [
  {
   "name": "Pat Freiermuth",
   "position": "TE",
   "nfl_team": "PIT",
   "proj": 8.32,
   "ros_rank": 122.0,
   "fp_waiver_rank": 8.0,
   "injury": "ACTIVE",
   "replaces": "Mason Taylor",
   "ros_rank_gain": 23.0,
   "week_proj_gain": -0.49,
   "priority": "MEDIUM",
   "availability": "ESPN_WAIVERS",
   "espn_pct_owned": 41.2,
   "fp_waiver_note": "With Colston Loveland and Dallas Goedert on bye in Week 10, some fantasy managers might be in search of a tight end to stream this week. Pat Freiermuth isn't having a banner season but could be a palatable option this week based on matchup.\n\nFreiermuth has been splitting TE targets with Darnell Washington and has an uninspiring 11.7% target share. Although Freiermuth has delivered five touchdowns (including one on a goal-line tush push), he's averaging 4.4 targets, 3.1 catches and 29.4 receiving yards per game.\n\nBut Freiermuth has a favorable Week 10 matchup against the Bengals. He had only 2-30-0 on four targets in a Week 6 game against Cincinnati, but Bengals defensive coordinator Al Golden's unit is usually content to give up receptions to tight ends over the middle.\n\nCincinnati entered Week 9 having allowed the ninth-most fantasy points to tight ends, even though no TE has scored a touchdown against the Bengals. Last year under Golden, the Bengals gave up the most catches, receiving yards and touchdowns to tight ends.\n\nLast week, the Titans' Gunnar Helm had a season-best 5-76-0 day against the Bengals. Helm hadn't produced more than 28 receiving yards in any other game this year.\n\nDespite his humble reception and yardage totals this season, Freiermuth has streaming appeal in Week 9."
  },
